<title>INDIA: Indian Sept 24-sector industrial output up 3.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Indian Sept 24-sector industrial output up 3.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's 24-sector industrial production index rose 3.2 percent in September over the same month in 1995, the Industry Ministry said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>    24-SECTOR INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION   Sep 96	Apr-Sep 96</p>
<p>    Coal					+8.0	     +8.7</p>
<p>    Crude petroleum			 -9.8	    -10.3</p>
<p>    Cement				    +4.3	    +12.2</p>
<p>    Saleable steel			  +1.2	     +4.0</p>
<p>    Electricity generation		+2.7	     +2.6</p>
<p>    Petroleum refinery products	 -9.9	     +4.3</p>
<p>    Steel ingots			   +12.4	     +5.5</p>
<p>    Nitrogenous fertiliser		-2.4	     -6.8</p>
<p>    Phosphatic fertiliser		 +2.9	     -9.1</p>
<p>    Saleable pig iron		    +46.9	    +23.2</p>
<p>    Aluminium				 +4.3	     -2.9</p>
<p>    Copper cathodes			+16.5	    -28.3</p>
<p>    Sugar				    -57.3	    +53.7</p>
<p>    Salt					 0.0	     +3.2</p>
<p>    Cloth-mill sector		    +21.4	     -0.8</p>
<p>    Cloth-decentralised sector	 +18.9	    +10.2</p>
<p>    Cotton yarn			    +11.4	     +3.2</p>
<p>    Jute manufacturers		   -19.9	    -15.4</p>
<p>    Commercial vehicles		   -7.8	    +12.8</p>
<p>    Cars					+6.4	    +18.7</p>
<p>    Jeeps				    +12.8	    +25.6</p>
<p>    Motor cycles			   +15.7	    +24.7</p>
<p>    Auto rickshaws			 +43.0	    +43.4</p>
<p>    Scooters/mopeds			 +8.9	    +21.2</p>
<p>    OVERALL				   +3.2	     +4.8</p>
<p>Note - The index includes 24 sectors accounting for 50.4 percent of the overall index of industrial production. The figures are preliminary.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
